Experiment 3 — Valid Arithmetic Expression
Aim

To write a program to recognize a valid arithmetic expression using the operators +, -, *, and / using FLEX and BISON.

Algorithm

FLEX:

Start the FLEX program.
Include the required header files.
Define regular expressions for identifiers, digits, and operators.
Return the appropriate tokens to BISON.
Ignore whitespace.
Return the end-of-input indication using yywrap().

BISON:
7. Define the required tokens.
8. Define operator associativity and precedence.
9. Define grammar rules for arithmetic expressions.
10. Call yyparse() to begin parsing.
11. If the input matches the grammar, recognize it as a valid expression.
12. If no grammar rule matches, call yyerror() and report an invalid expression.
13. Stop.

Pseudocode
START

FLEX:
    Define tokens:
        ID
        DIGIT
        Operators

    Read input expression

    Convert lexemes into tokens
    Pass tokens to BISON

BISON:
    Define grammar:

    Expression → Expression + Expression
               | Expression - Expression
               | Expression * Expression
               | Expression / Expression
               | - Expression
               | ( Expression )
               | DIGIT
               | ID

    Set operator precedence

    Start parsing

    IF expression matches grammar:
        Print "Valid Expression"
    ELSE:
        Print "Invalid Expression"

STOP
